@startuml 04-app-lab-effect-cycle
skinparam backgroundColor white
title Rastok — one outbound Call, real or scripted world
skinparam shadowing false

actor Caller
participant "Hosted runner / Lab" as Entry
participant "Core VM / DriverPoller" as Core
database "Journal" as Journal
participant "Bound Driver" as Driver
participant "External system" as World

Caller -> Entry: execute checked plan
Entry -> Core: inject explicit typed input
Core -> Core: prepare identity, routes and capacity
Core -> Journal: commit INGRESS + selected routes
Core -> Core: consume ready work; prepare exact request
Core -> Journal: commit EGRESS open before any effect

alt real Driver
  Core -> Driver: start committed Call intent
  Driver -> World: perform effect
  World --> Driver: physical outcome
else Lab Driver
  Core -> Driver: same committed intent and Contract
  Driver -> Driver: select scripted outcome / remain silent
end

Driver --> Core: correlated typed completion
Core -> Core: validate Contract; select routes; reserve capacity
Core -> Journal: close EGRESS once; commit completion transition
Core -> Core: publish ordered frames / terminal and deliveries
Core --> Entry: recorded state and causal evidence
Entry --> Caller: result / report / read-only projection

note over Core,Journal
If capacity is unavailable, no partial publication.
A timeout is a scheduler decision, not a Driver reply.
An outbound result is not a new INGRESS root.
end note
note over Driver,World
Drivers never assign envelope identities or write journal records.
Recovery never blindly repeats the physical effect.
end note
@enduml
